<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Saddam Hussein</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1937–2006</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Saddam Hussein was the Ba'athist ruler of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq</a>, effective leader from the 1970s and president from 1979 to 2003. His dictatorship relied on the security services and repression, including the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anfal-campaign">Anfal campaign</a> against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kurds">Kurds</a>. He led Iraq into war with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a> (1980–1988) and the invasion of Kuwait in 1990. He was overthrown by the US-led invasion of 2003 and executed in 2006.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/saddam-hussein.jpg" alt="Saddam Hussein" width="320" height="423" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Iraqi News Agency · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Saddam_Hussein_in_1998.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
